      "math_academy_id": "e-12766",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14274148/assets/45a423930fb07c365f10cdfbdeb3d45ef337078fa77e1b0699388088438d4c70.png)\n\n \n\nWhat is the subset $A$ of $U=\\{ 1,2,3,4,5 \\}$ whose indicator function $\\boldsymbol{1}_A(x)$ is shown above?",
      "worked_solution": "An indicator function maps elements from a set to the values $0$ or $1,$ depending on whether the element belongs to a specified subset. The indicator function is designed to \"indicate\" whether an element is a member of a subset.\n\nMore specifically, consider a universal set $X.$ Then, the indicator function of a set $A \\subseteq X$ is the function\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14274148/assets/0e1615637e17e897abd3747198e99447dc0ce971a80c2783b74c54c100af38bf.svg)\n\nIn the diagram above, only the elements $1,2,$ and $5$ are mapped to $1.$ Therefore, the indicator function in the diagram above corresponds to the set $A=\\{ 1,2,5 \\}.$",
